1.1 Obtaining Emacsvox
======================

Before beginning, install ‘git’, ‘make’, GNU Texinfo (which provides
‘makeinfo’), and Emacs 31 or newer
(https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/download.html).  The Speech Backends
chapter lists the additional platform prerequisites for the recommended
Omnivox server.

   The maintained source is <https://github.com/bartbunting/emacsvox>.
Clone it into the permanent directory where it will be used:

     git clone https://github.com/bartbunting/emacsvox
     cd emacsvox

   The checkout itself is the source-checkout installation.  The build
operates in place; it does not create a second directory to copy
elsewhere.


File: emacsvox.info,  Node: Quick Installation,  Next: Confirming First Speech,  Prev: Obtaining Emacsvox,  Up: Installation

1.2 First Speech Checklist
==========================

  1. Select Emacs 31 or newer.  If it is not the system ‘emacs’, copy
     ‘local.mk.example’ to the ignored ‘local.mk’ and set ‘EMACS’:

          EMACS=/path/to/emacs-31/bin/emacs

     Verify the selection before diagnosing a compiler failure:

          make check-emacs

  2. Configure and compile the checkout:

          make all

     Do not compile Emacsvox with an older system Emacs.  Tests prefer
     source and therefore do not prove that the byte-code used by a
     normal startup is current.

  3. Install the recommended Omnivox speech server.  *Note Speech
     Backends::, for the supported platform matrix, exact prerequisite
     classes, source and WSL2 build paths, and compatibility
     alternatives.

  4. Run the non-audible launcher preflight from the Emacsvox checkout:

          ./bin/emacsvox --diagnose

     It validates the checkout, Emacs, and backend without playing
     audio, creating an Omnivox session log, or opening interactive
     Emacs.  Before continuing, confirm that its report includes Emacs
     31 or newer, the ‘omnivox’ speech backend, and an isolated ‘-Q’
     startup.  Correct any path or version error that it prints.

  5. Run the deliberately audible backend check:

          ./bin/emacsvox --check

     The launcher prints its selections and explicitly announces that
     the audible check is starting.  Continue only after hearing both
     the tone and speech.  Do not diagnose Emacs configuration until
     this standalone Omnivox check passes.

  6. Prove a clean Emacsvox start:

          ./bin/emacsvox

     The launcher defaults to Omnivox, uses the selected Emacs 31 or
     newer, and loads the setup source by its absolute path.  The
     session uses ‘-Q’: it loads neither site files nor a personal Emacs
     init file.  This makes first speech a reproducible installation
     proof rather than a side effect of existing configuration.

     ‘./bin/emacsvox --diagnose’ prints the selected root, setup source,
     Emacs version, and backend without playing audio or starting
     interactive Emacs.  ‘./bin/emacsvox --help’ documents explicit
     ‘EMACS’, ‘TTS_PROGRAM’, and ‘EMACSVOX_DIR’ overrides.  Arguments
     after ‘--’ are passed to Emacs.


File: emacsvox.info,  Node: Confirming First Speech,  Next: Recovering From No Speech,  Prev: Quick Installation,  Up: Installation

1.3 Confirming First Speech
===========================

A successful isolated start speaks a versioned introduction ending with:

     I am completely operational, and all my circuits are functioning
     perfectly!

   The preceding overview key and version number can change.  The
sentence above is the stable first-speech checkpoint.  A startup
auditory icon may also play, but it depends on optional audio support
and is not part of acceptance.

   Before changing personal configuration, make these checks in the
isolated session:

  1. Type ‘M-x tts-speak-version RET’.  The live speech adapter should
     speak its version response.
  2. Type ‘C-h v tts-program RET’.  The displayed current value should
     name ‘omnivox’.
  3. Use ‘C-n’ and ‘C-p’ to move over lines and confirm ordinary spoken
     navigation.  Type ‘M-x emacsvox-describe-emacsvox RET’ for the
     Emacsvox overview.  *Note Basic Usage::, for the tested starter
     commands.

   Only after these checks pass is the isolated first-use proof
complete.


